282 0 obj
<< /A 770 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart illustrating a medical data process. The user provides input to the Information Collection Agent, which stores data in a database. The Diagnosis Agent queries the database, then suggests diagnoses to the Treatment Plan Agent. The Treatment Plan Agent updates or consults guidelines in the database and returns a personalized treatment plan to the user.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a medical data process. The user provides input to the Information Collection Agent, which stores data in a database. The Diagnosis Agent queries the database, then suggests diagnoses to the Treatment Plan Agent. The Treatment Plan Agent updates or consults guidelines in the database and returns a personalized treatment plan to the user.\r\n) /K 0 /P 143 0 R /Pg 271 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
283 0 obj
<< /A 771 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart illustrating an information processing system. A user/system provides text and files to an Information Collection Agent, which interacts with multiple components: GPT-4 for JSON parsing, spaCy for UMLS mapping, Image Analysis for OCR insights, PDF Analysis for extracting text, and MongoDB for data storage. Each component processes information and sends data back to the agent, which stores or updates patient info and merges updates.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart illustrating an information processing system. A user/system provides text and files to an Information Collection Agent, which interacts with multiple components: GPT-4 for JSON parsing, spaCy for UMLS mapping, Image Analysis for OCR insights, PDF Analysis for extracting text, and MongoDB for data storage. Each component processes information and sends data back to the agent, which stores or updates patient info and merges updates.\r\n) /K 0 /P 143 0 R /Pg 272 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
284 0 obj
<< /A 772 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart depicting a medical data processing system. It starts with user input \(text, images, PDFs\) analyzed by the Information Collection Agent, which passes symptoms and features to the Diagnosis Agent. The Diagnosis Agent provides candidate diagnoses to the Treatment Plan Agent, which updates diagnosis info. The system stores data and updates treatment records in a Database/Knowledge Base. Ultimately, it provides a personalized treatment plan to the user.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart depicting a medical data processing system. It starts with user input \(text, images, PDFs\) analyzed by the Information Collection Agent, which passes symptoms and features to the Diagnosis Agent. The Diagnosis Agent provides candidate diagnoses to the Treatment Plan Agent, which updates diagnosis info. The system stores data and updates treatment records in a Database/Knowledge Base. Ultimately, it provides a personalized treatment plan to the user.\r\n) /K 0 /P 143 0 R /Pg 273 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
285 0 obj
<< /A 773 0 R /ActualText (Bar chart comparing the top-1 accuracy of different models and methods. GPT-3.5-turbo and GPT-4 show around 0.4 accuracy. GPT-4-turbo and GPT-4.0-mini have lower accuracy near 0.2. GPT-4.0 reaches about 0.6. Cohere and baseline\(1/r\) are near 0.35, while "ours aggregator" has the highest accuracy at 0.8.\r\n) /Alt (Bar chart comparing the top-1 accuracy of different models and methods. GPT-3.5-turbo and GPT-4 show around 0.4 accuracy. GPT-4-turbo and GPT-4.0-mini have lower accuracy near 0.2. GPT-4.0 reaches about 0.6. Cohere and baseline\(1/r\) are near 0.35, while "ours aggregator" has the highest accuracy at 0.8.\r\n) /K 0 /P 143 0 R /Pg 274 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
286 0 obj
<< /A 774 0 R /ActualText (Scatter plot showing the relationship between reliability on the calibration set \(x-axis\) and accuracy on the test set \(y-axis\) for different models. Models include gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini, gpt-4-turbo, gpt-3.5-turbo, gpt-4, and cohere. Points vary in position, with gpt-4 achieving the highest reliability and test accuracy.\r\n) /Alt (Scatter plot showing the relationship between reliability on the calibration set \(x-axis\) and accuracy on the test set \(y-axis\) for different models. Models include gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini, gpt-4-turbo, gpt-3.5-turbo, gpt-4, and cohere. Points vary in position, with gpt-4 achieving the highest reliability and test accuracy.\r\n) /K 0 /P 143 0 R /Pg 275 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
287 0 obj
<< /A 775 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart illustrating a diagnostic process using AI models. It starts with patient data including text descriptions and optional image paths. The text is processed by multiple large language models \(gpt-3.5, gpt-4, cohere\) providing probabilistic disease predictions. Images are analyzed by an image model \(ResNet18\). Outputs are merged in a fusion module, generating a combined probability distribution for a final diagnosis across five diseases.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a diagnostic process using AI models. It starts with patient data including text descriptions and optional image paths. The text is processed by multiple large language models \(gpt-3.5, gpt-4, cohere\) providing probabilistic disease predictions. Images are analyzed by an image model \(ResNet18\). Outputs are merged in a fusion module, generating a combined probability distribution for a final diagnosis across five diseases.\r\n) /K 0 /P 143 0 R /Pg 278 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
288 0 obj
<< /A 776 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart illustrating a process for collecting patient information via a public API. Key steps include parsing patient descriptions using GPT-4, standardizing terms with scispaCy and UMLS, inserting or merging records in MongoDB, handling file paths to extract image or PDF text insights, and storing results in GridFS. The process ends with returning structured data in JSON format.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a process for collecting patient information via a public API. Key steps include parsing patient descriptions using GPT-4, standardizing terms with scispaCy and UMLS, inserting or merging records in MongoDB, handling file paths to extract image or PDF text insights, and storing results in GridFS. The process ends with returning structured data in JSON format.\r\n) /K 1 /P 143 0 R /Pg 278 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
